    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d474">

                <pb facs="0440" n="324" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg324"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.7111/58.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Ambassador Page.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 186.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-03-09">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 9, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your
                    despatches Nos. 251 and 252, of February 21 and 23, respectively, in which you
                    enclose copies of notes received by you from the British Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs asking that steps be taken to prevent the departure for the Gold Coast
                    Colony of the followers of one “Chief Sam,” who claims to be an African
                    chief.</p>
                <p>The Department has transmitted copies of your despatches to the Governor of
                    Oklahoma, the Attorney General and the Postmaster General and has been informed
                    by the Attorney General that his Department is unable to take any action against
                    “Chief Sam.” The Post Office Department, however, is making an investigation of
                    the matter to determine whether “Chief Sam “has made fraudulent use of the
                    United States mails.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">John E. Osborne</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
